I usually try to get to minetown first just to get to an altar (any
altar will do - by the time I get there I usually have a bunch of
stuff I want to BUC test).

Hiding behind your pet - or even letting the pet distract everyone
while you make your escape - is quite vital.  I often lose pets who
valiantly stand against my opponents for me.  Kinda coldhearted, I
guess, but it's better than losing a pet because it fell into a spiked
pit.

Writing a certain word repeatedly in the dust also buys time for your
life to regenerate.  And when I say repeatedly, I really mean so often
that you can type it in with your eyes closed at 3am in the morning.

In any case, unless you successfully pull off the protection racket,
don't try to explore too much after minetown - mine's end
occassionally has nasties already, including vampires in one variant.
After getting to minetown and checking out the shops for a magic lamp
and useful tools, as well as BUC testing at the temple, you can go up
and explore the main dungeon again.

If your problem is that you can't even reach minetown - hide behind
your pet or write the word.  The word is your friend in the mines.



